{"name":"Zappy Zebra","hex":"#f1f3f3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zappy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lively or energetic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zappy"},{"term":"zebra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of three species of subgenus Hippotigris: Equus grevyi, Equus quagga, or Equus zebra, all with black and white stripes and native to Africa.","A referee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zebra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zolpidem","blocks":[{"text":"Zolpidem, sold under the brand name Ambien among others, is a medication primarily used for the short-term treatment of sleeping problems. Guidelines recommend that it be used only after cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia and after behavioral changes, such as sleep hygiene, have been tried. It decreases the time to sleep onset by about fifteen minutes and at larger doses helps people stay asleep longer. It is taken by mouth and is available as conventional tablets, extended-release tablets, or sublingual tablets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Zolpidem2DACS.svg/330px-Zolpidem2DACS.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zolpidem"},{"title":"Zebra","blocks":[{"text":"Zebras are African equines with distinctive black-and-white striped coats. There are three living species: Grévy's zebra, the plains zebra, and the mountain zebra. Zebras share the genus Equus with horses and asses, the three groups being the only living members of the family Equidae. Zebra stripes come in different patterns, unique to each individual. Several theories have been proposed for the function of these patterns, with most evidence supporting them as a deterrent for biting flies. Zebras inhabit eastern and southern Africa and can be found in a variety of habitats such as savannahs, grasslands, woodlands, shrublands, and mountainous areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Plains_Zebra_Equus_quagga_cropped.jpg/330px-Plains_Zebra_Equus_quagga_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zebra"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Zolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png/500px-Zolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Zolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png/1280px-Zolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Zolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png/500px-Zolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZolpidem_ball-and-stick_model.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Kc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg/500px-Kc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Kc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg/1280px-Kc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Kc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg/500px-Kc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Generic zolpidem tartrate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKc-zolpidem-10mg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Ambien-pictures.jpg/250px-Ambien-pictures.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/Ambien-pictures.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unsc